<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 40 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 40 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 40 million stg of unspecified late assistance.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    700 MLN    750 MLN    700 MLN    700 MLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    411 MLN    661 MLN    701 MLN</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	    161 MLN    108 MLN    =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   =	    250 MLN*   142 MLN    =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED ASSISTANCE	    =	    =	     40 MLN</p>
<p> * INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
